-- title:
--   Primes over varpi in the finite chart: minimal or maximal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` structure) and let $\varpi \in R$ be an element whose span is the maximal ideal, $\mathfrak m_R = (\varpi)$. Let $K_0$ be a field realised as the fraction field of $R$, and let $F$ be a field that is an $R$- and $K_0$-algebra compatibly (a scalar tower $R \to K_0 \to F$). Let $j \in F$ be nonzero, transcendental over $R$, and suppose $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ generated by $j$ over $K_0$. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the subalgebra `chartAlg R F {j}` of $F$, namely the set of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ containing the image of $\varpi$ under $R \to A$, either $\mathfrak q$ is a minimal prime over the principal ideal generated by that image, or $\mathfrak q$ is maximal.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre of the finite ($j$-)chart of the two-chart integral model is one-dimensional: modulo $\varpi$ the chart ring has Krull dimension at most one, so a point of the special fibre is either a generic point of a branch or a closed point. It feeds the analysis of the two-chart model and of its modular-curve instances, for instance the descent statements about maximal ideals of the chart ring and the construction of normal proper models of relative dimension one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_mem_minimalPrimes_or_isMaximal_of_mem_chartAlgFin.lean

